  "name": "rust-incidents",
  "description": "An experimental Rust library exploring advanced error handling patterns, emphasizing stack trace capture and result size optimization. It implements a heap-allocated failure wrapper that provides Python-style tracebacks in debug builds while maintaining a zero-cost boxed representation in release mode. The project introduces custom traits for error interoperability and automated conversion, aiming to inform future Rust RFCs regarding diagnostic ergonomics.",
